Modifications to marked.esm.js in this fork (speed only; no output change):

- Inline tokenizer dispatch: the escape, tag, link, reflink, emStrong,
  codespan, br, del and autolink tokenizers first check the input's first
  character and return at once when it is not one their pattern can start
  with, instead of running the pattern to failure.
- lheading: the composed setext-heading pattern is not run when the input
  contains no newline (it cannot match then).
- Lexer.lex: the carriage-return normalisation is skipped when the input
  contains no carriage return.
- Emphasis masking: for an inline segment containing no '*', '_' or '~',
  the closer-index precomputation is skipped (emStrong/del can never match
  there, and the indices are recomputed on demand if ever consulted); the
  two masking replaces are skipped when the segment contains no backtick,
  backslash, '[' or '<' and no emStrongMask hook is set — neither pattern
  can match such a segment.
- The options.extensions lookups (block, inline, renderers, startBlock,
  startInline) are read once per lex/parse call instead of once per token,
  and the tokenizer reference is held in a local in the lex loops.
- list(): first lines are taken with indexOf/slice rather than split with
  a limit.

The repository's parse.js also drives this fork's Lexer and Parser
directly on a shared, pre-wired options object (with one Lexer/Parser pair
reused under a constructor-exact state reset) instead of paying
marked.parse()'s per-call setup.
